course: dictionary
lesson: 10059
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around the word, because they are its context. «In the testudo, or tortoise formation, soldiers locked their shields above and around them to protect against arrows.» The clues are soldiers, shields and arrows, so this testudo is a Roman army formation, not an animal.
explain: The sentence gives you a second clue. The words «or tortoise formation» tell you that testudo is a Latin word meaning tortoise. The soldiers' shields look like a tortoise's shell, so the formation has that name.
explain: In a science text, the same word means something different. Testudo is the scientific name of a group of tortoises. Ask yourself what the topic is, then pick the meaning that fits. Then swap it into the sentence to check.
fact: Testudo is the Latin word for tortoise.
fact: As a history word, «testudo» means a Roman army formation where soldiers held their shields over their heads and around them, like a tortoise's shell.
fact: As a science word, «Testudo» is the name of a group of tortoises, such as the Greek tortoise and Hermann's tortoise.
fact: The topic of the text tells you which meaning to choose.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The soldiers formed a testudo and moved slowly up to the enemy wall.» What does testudo mean here? | A kind of Roman bread | A pet tortoise kept in a garden | A tall tower on a hill | *A protective formation of shields held by soldiers
exercise: Which animal belongs to the genus Testudo? | The arrow | A garden snail | The Roman soldier | *The Greek tortoise
exercise: In «the testudo, or tortoise formation», which English word tells you what testudo means? | arrows | shields | soldiers | *tortoise
test: Which meaning fits testudo in a history lesson? | A pet kept in a shed | A type of sandwich | *A Roman shield formation, like a tortoise shell | A tall mountain
test: Why did the testudo protect Roman soldiers? | They were wearing bright paint | They ran away very fast | They could hide in a cave | *Shields over their heads and around them stopped arrows and stones
exam: In «Hermann's tortoise belongs to the genus Testudo», what does Testudo mean? | A Roman soldier | A battle with arrows | A shield held over the head | *A group of tortoises, such as Hermann's tortoise
